From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lauri Nomme <lauri.nomme@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0300
Subject: net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: allocate NAPI dummy device before netdev registration

The netdevs share one DMA ring and one NAPI set, carried by an internal
dummy netdevice (eth->dummy_dev). mtk_probe() currently allocates that
dummy device only AFTER registering the netdevs, leaving a window where a
netdev is already visible to the network core / netifd while eth->dummy_dev
is still NULL.

netifd brings the first netdev up the moment it is registered; mtk_open()
then runs mtk_dma_init() -> mtk_rx_alloc() -> __xdp_rxq_info_reg(), which
sees eth->dummy_dev == NULL and fires

  WARNING: CPU: ... Missing net_device from driver   (net/core/xdp.c)

returning -ENODEV. mtk_open() fails and the interface (observed as WAN eth1
on BPI-R4 Pro 8X) stays down until manually reopened once probe has
finished.

Close the race by allocating the dummy device (and adding the shared
tx/rx NAPI onto it) before the netdevs are registered, and free it from the
probe error path instead of the now-unneeded err_unreg_netdev cleanup.

Variant for the RSS/multi-ring tree: same reorder against the mtk_probe()
tail as modified by the multi-ring NAPI/RSS patch (eth->irq_fe, per-ring
rx_napi[] + MTK_RSS ring add). Also reroute the dummy-allocation-failure
goto to err_deinit_ppe (err_unreg_netdev label is removed).
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c | 42 ++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -6396,28 +6396,18 @@ static int mtk_probe(struct platform_dev
 
 	eth->rx_buf_len = MTK_MAX_RX_LENGTH;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < MTK_MAX_DEVS; i++) {
-		if (!eth->netdev[i])
-			continue;
-
-		err = register_netdev(eth->netdev[i]);
-		if (err) {
-			dev_err(eth->dev, "error bringing up device\n");
-			goto err_deinit_ppe;
-		} else
-			netif_info(eth, probe, eth->netdev[i],
-				   "mediatek frame engine at 0x%08lx, irq %d\n",
-				   eth->netdev[i]->base_addr, eth->irq_fe[MTK_FE_IRQ_SHARED]);
-	}
-
 	/* we run 2 devices on the same DMA ring so we need a dummy device
-	 * for NAPI to work
+	 * for NAPI to work. Allocate it before registering the netdevs so a
+	 * concurrent ndo_open (netifd bringing up WAN the moment a netdev is
+	 * registered) never observes eth->dummy_dev == NULL, which would make
+	 * mtk_rx_alloc() -> __xdp_rxq_info_reg() WARN (net/core/xdp.c
+	 * "Missing net_device from driver") and leave the interface down.
 	 */
 	eth->dummy_dev = alloc_netdev_dummy(0);
 	if (!eth->dummy_dev) {
 		err = -ENOMEM;
 		dev_err(eth->dev, "failed to allocated dummy device\n");
-		goto err_unreg_netdev;
+		goto err_deinit_ppe;
 	}
 	eth->dummy_dev->threaded = 1;
 	strcpy(eth->dummy_dev->name, "mtk_eth");
@@ -6430,15 +6420,29 @@ static int mtk_probe(struct platform_dev
 				       mtk_napi_rx);
 	}
 
+	for (i = 0; i < MTK_MAX_DEVS; i++) {
+		if (!eth->netdev[i])
+			continue;
+
+		err = register_netdev(eth->netdev[i]);
+		if (err) {
+			dev_err(eth->dev, "error bringing up device\n");
+			goto err_deinit_ppe;
+		} else
+			netif_info(eth, probe, eth->netdev[i],
+				   "mediatek frame engine at 0x%08lx, irq %d\n",
+				   eth->netdev[i]->base_addr, eth->irq_fe[MTK_FE_IRQ_SHARED]);
+	}
+
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, eth);
 	schedule_delayed_work(&eth->reset.monitor_work,
 			      MTK_DMA_MONITOR_TIMEOUT);
 
 	return 0;
 
-err_unreg_netdev:
-	mtk_unreg_dev(eth);
 err_deinit_ppe:
+	if (eth->dummy_dev)
+		free_netdev(eth->dummy_dev);
 	mtk_ppe_deinit(eth);
 	mtk_mdio_cleanup(eth);
 err_free_dev:
